## §0.1 Lessons Retrieved
  ☐ READ: _project/lessons/patterns/stock-reservation-checkout.md (High)
    → Prevention: ifRevisionId MANDATORY, rollback on ANY Stripe failure, reservedStock release NOT stock
  ☐ READ: _project/lessons/patterns/bus-stop-debugging-methodology.md (Critical)
    → Prevention: Trace end-to-end → verify each bus stop → isolate broken stop → fix
  ☐ READ: _project/lessons/workflows/pre-flight-baseline-check.md (High)
    → Prevention: Always verify baseline build before sprint work
  ☐ READ: _project/lessons/workflows/command-singular-focus.md (High)
    → Prevention: /sprint plans, /implement executes, /test verifies
  ☐ READ: _project/lessons/workflows/velocity-aware-sprint-planning.md (High)
    → Prevention: Compressed context → tight sprint doc → single execution → fast review
  ☐ READ: _project/lessons/anti-patterns/implementation-first-debugging.md (Critical)
    → Prevention: Never implement before tracing complete flow

## §0.2 Pre-Flight Checklist
  ☐ Branch check: `git status` → verify on correct branch
  ☐ Baseline build: `npm run build` → document PASS/FAIL
    If FAIL: document pre-existing failures BEFORE sprint work
  ☐ Stripe CLI running: `stripe listen --forward-to localhost:3000/api/webhook`
  ☐ Dev server running: `npm run dev` → http://localhost:3000 responds
  ☐ Scope lock: confirm no other sprint in progress

## §0.3 Active Constraint Rules (from Lessons)
  CONSTRAINT-1: ifRevisionId is MANDATORY on all Sanity stock patches
  CONSTRAINT-2: Trace complete data flow before writing any test logic
  CONSTRAINT-3: Never assume field types — read schema/types first
  CONSTRAINT-4: Pre-flight build baseline before every Scope Contract
  CONSTRAINT-5: Single responsibility — /implement executes, /test verifies

